grow:
Design a career skill tree for a high school student exploring "{{topic}}". Reply with only JSON in this shape:
{"name":"Short path name","blurb":"One sentence about the career.","weights":{"logic":0-3,"tech":0-3,"science":0-3,"creativity":0-3,"charisma":0-3,"empathy":0-3,"craft":0-3},"nodes":[{"id":"n1","t":0,"title":"2-4 words","learn":"1-2 sentences on what is learned","objective":"One concrete, checkable task a teen can do for free","req":[],"res":[{"name":"Resource name","url":"https://..."}]}]}
Rules: 6 to 8 nodes. "t" is the tier 0-3 (0 = start in grade 9-10, 3 = grade 12/first year). Tier 0 has 1 node with req []. Every other node lists 1-2 ids from lower tiers in "req". Give each node 1-2 FREE resources, only from well-known sites whose URLs you are confident exist (Khan Academy, MIT OpenCourseWare, OpenStax, freeCodeCamp, Kaggle Learn, CS50, Crash Course, official organization sites). You may add a final node with "branch" set to one of these existing path ids if a natural specialization link exists: {{pathIds}}.
Student context: {{context}}

reflect:
A student using Edventure shared a recent change in their life, results or perspective. Read it with empathy and suggest how their career skill-tree journey should adapt. Reply with only JSON in this shape:
{"summary":"2-3 warm sentences that acknowledge what happened and reframe it constructively","signals":{"more":["stat ids they now lean toward"],"less":["stat ids they lean away from"]},"keep":[{"id":"path id","note":"why it may still fit, or how to reshape it"}],"pause":[{"id":"path id","note":"why it's okay to step back for now"}],"add":[{"id":"path id","why":"why it fits what they shared"}],"grow":[{"name":"New career path name","why":"why it fits"}],"firstStep":{"pathId":"path id","title":"2-5 words","objective":"one small, concrete, encouraging task they can do this week for free"}}
Rules: Use only these existing path ids for keep, pause, add and firstStep: {{pathIds}}. Their names: {{pathNames}}. Only put paths currently on their journey in keep or pause: {{journey}}. add: 1-3 existing paths that are NOT on their journey. grow: 0-2 careers that are not in the existing list at all and clearly fit what they shared. Stat ids: logic, tech, science, creativity, charisma, empathy, craft. Never shame the student: treat failing a course or changing their mind as useful information. Remind them that progress is never lost. Don't promise admissions, grades or job outcomes.
